.TH "dotnet-package-update" "1" "2025-10-31" "" ".NET Documentation"
.hy
.SH dotnet package update
.PP
\f[B]This article applies to:\f[R] \[u2714]\[uFE0F] .NET 10 SDK and later versions
.SH NAME
.PP
dotnet-package-update - Update referenced packages in a project.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package update [<packages>...]
    [--interactive] [--project <path>]
    [--verbosity <level>] [--vulnerable]

dotnet package update -h|--help
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \f[V]dotnet package update\f[R] command updates packages used by projects.
If NuGetAudit is enabled, it can also attempt to automatically update update packages with known vulnerabilities to fixed versions.
.SS Warnings as Errors
.PP
\f[V]dotnet package update\f[R] does implicit restores to check if the resulting package graph is free of errors.
Using \f[V]--vulnerable\f[R] also does an implicit restore to find NuGetAudit warnings.
However, if your project uses \f[V]WarningsAsErrors\f[R] or \f[V]TreatWarningsAsErrors\f[R], NuGet\[cq]s restore warnings can cause restore to fail, preventing the update from completing.
.PP
We recommend taking advantage of MSBuild conditions and environment variables as a workaround until this feature request (https://github.com/NuGet/Home/issues/14311) is implemented.
For example, set \f[V]<TreatWarningsAsErrors Condition=\[dq] \[aq]$(CustomCondition)\[aq] == \[aq]\[aq]>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>\f[R] in your project, and then on most Linux and Mac shells you can run \f[V]CustomCondition=true dotnet package update\f[R].
On Windows Command Prompt and PowerShell, you will need to set the environment variable, run dotnet package update, then unset the environment variable as three separate commands.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]packages\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
An optional list of packages to update.
When no packages are provided, the command will attempt to update all packages referenced by the project.
Packages can be a package name optionally followed by an \f[V]\[at]\f[R] and a version number.
For example, \f[V]dotnet package update Contoso.Utilities\f[R] or \f[V]dotnet package update Contoso.Utilities\[at]3.2.1\f[R].
When no version is provided, it will find the highest version available on the configured package sources.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--interactive\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Allows the command to stop and wait for user input or action (for example to complete authentication).
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--project <path>\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
The project which packages should be updated in.
If a directory is provided, it searches for project and solution files in the directory.
Defaults to the current working directory.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--verbosity\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Display this amount of details in the output: \f[V][n]ormal\f[R], \f[V][m]inimal\f[R], \f[V][q]uiet\f[R], \f[V][d]etailed\f[R], or \f[V][diag]nostic\f[R].
The default is \f[V]normal\f[R].
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]--vulnerable\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
If restore reports any packages as having known vulnerabilities, this command will upgrade those packages.
Using this option will upgrade packages to the lowest version that is higher than the currently referenced version, that does not have any known vulnerabilities.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\f[VB]-?|-h|--help\f[B]\f[R]
.RS 2
.PP
Prints out a description of how to use the command.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP \[bu] 2
Update all packages in the project to the highest version available
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package update
\f[R]
.fi
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
Updating outdated packages in S:\[rs]src\[rs]test\[rs]update\[rs]ConsoleApp1.
  ConsoleApp1:
    Updated Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration 9.0.0 to 9.0.9.
    Updated Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection 9.0.0 to 9.0.9.

Updated 2 packages in 7 scanned packages.
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Update Contoso.Utilities to the highest version available, and Fabrikam.WebApi to version 1.2.3
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package update Contoso.Utilities Fabrikam.WebApi\[at]1.2.3
\f[R]
.fi
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
Updating outdated packages in S:\[rs]src\[rs]test\[rs]update\[rs]ConsoleApp1.
  ConsoleApp1:
    Updated Contoso.Utilities 2.3.1 to 2.4.6.
    Updated Fabrikam.WebApi 1.0.2 to 1.2.3.

Updated 2 packages in 2 scanned packages.
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Update packages with known vulnerabilities
.RS 2
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
dotnet package update --vulnerable
\f[R]
.fi
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
Updating packages with security advisories in S:\[rs]src\[rs]test\[rs]update\[rs]ConsoleApp1
  ConsoleApp1:
    Updating System.Text.Json 8.0.0 to 8.0.5.

Updated 1 packages in 31 scanned packages.
\f[R]
.fi
.RE
